doctype html
html(lang="en")
    head
        meta(charset="UTF-8")
        title Currency API Documentation (Version 0 – Under Development)
    body
        h1 Currency API Documentation
        p Base URL:
            strong #{baseUrl}
        p
            | This API provides a comprehensive set of endpoints to manage currency exchange rates. It allows users to add, retrieve, and delete rates.
            | The API supports filtering based on uploader, source, currency code, and date. Additionally, it provides computed percentage changes between successive rates for the same currency.

        h2 Authentication
        p
            | Certain endpoints, specifically POST and DELETE operations, require authentication via JWT (JSON Web Token).
            | Include your token in the
            strong Authorization
            |  header as follows:
        pre Authorization: Bearer &lt;your_jwt_token&gt;

        h2 Endpoints

        h3 0. Retrieve Unique Uploaders and Sources for a Currency
        p
            | This endpoint returns a list of unique combinations of uploaders and sources that have provided exchange rates for the specified currency.
            | It allows clients to identify all contributors and the sources they utilized for a particular currency.
        p
            strong GET /findUploader&Source/:currencyCode
        p Example URL:
            strong
                a(href="#{baseUrl}findUploader&Source/USD") #{baseUrl}findUploader&Source/USD

        p Response:
            | Each item in the response includes:
        ul
            li currencyCode: | The ISO currency code (e.g., USD, EUR).
            li currencyName: | The full name of the currency.
            li uploadedBy: | The name of the user who submitted the rate.
            li source: | The origin or source of the currency rate.
        p Notes:
        ul
            li Performs a **case-insensitive** match on the currency code.
            li Groups results by both uploader and source to avoid duplicates.
            li Results are sorted alphabetically by `uploadedBy` and then by `source`.
            li Returns HTTP 404 if no matching combinations are found.

        h3 1. Retrieve All Uploaders
        p
            | Retrieves a complete list of all users who have submitted currency exchange rates.
            | This endpoint provides an overview of contributors within the system.
        p
            strong GET /uploaderList
        p Example URL:
            strong
                a(href="#{baseUrl}uploaderList") #{baseUrl}uploaderList

        p Response:
            | Each item includes:
        ul
            li uploadedBy: | The name of the uploader.
        p Notes:
        ul
            li Results are sorted alphabetically by `uploadedBy`.
            li Returns HTTP 404 if no uploaders exist in the system.

        h3 2. Retrieve Sources by Uploader
        p
            | This endpoint fetches all sources associated with a specific uploader.
            | It allows clients to understand which sources were used by a particular contributor to submit currency rates.
        p
            strong GET /sourceList?uploader=&lt;uploader&gt;
        p Example URL:
            strong
                a(href="#{baseUrl}sourceList?uploader=admin123") #{baseUrl}sourceList?uploader=admin123

        p Response:
            | Each item contains:
        ul
            li source: | The name of the source.
        p Notes:
        ul
            li If the `uploader` parameter is omitted, a default uploader is used.
            li The match on the uploader is case-insensitive.
            li Returns HTTP 404 if no sources are found for the specified uploader.

        h3 3. Retrieve Currencies by Source and Uploader
        p
            | Retrieves all currencies that a specific uploader has submitted under a particular source.
            | This endpoint helps clients identify which currencies are available from a given source for a contributor.
        p
            strong GET /currencyList?source=&lt;source&gt;&uploader=&lt;uploader&gt;
        p Example URL:
            strong
                a(href="#{baseUrl}currencyList?source=MM Exchange&uploader=admin123") #{baseUrl}currencyList?source=MM Exchange&uploader=admin123

        p Response:
            | Each item contains:
        ul
            li currencyCode: | ISO currency code (e.g., USD, EUR).
            li currencyName: | The full name of the currency.
        p Notes:
        ul
            li Performs **case-insensitive** matching for both `source` and `uploader`.
            li Results are sorted alphabetically by `currencyCode`.

        h3 4. Add a New Currency Rate (JWT Required)
        p
            | Allows an authenticated user to add a new currency rate to the system.
            | Upon successful addition, a Socket.IO event is emitted to notify subscribers in real-time.
        p
            strong POST /add
        p Example URL:
            strong
                a(href="#{baseUrl}add") #{baseUrl}add

        p Request Body (Required Fields):
        ul
            li currencyCode (string): | ISO code of the currency (e.g., USD, EUR).
            li unit (number): | The unit value for the currency rate.
            li buyRate (number): | Buying rate of the currency.
            li sellRate (number): | Selling rate of the currency.
            li uploadedDate (YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm:ss): | Timestamp of the rate submission. Must not be in the future.
            li source (string): | Source of the currency rate.
        p Notes:
        ul
            li Returns HTTP 400 if any required fields are missing or the date format is invalid.
            li Returns HTTP 409 if an identical rate already exists for the same uploader, source, and currency.
            li Emits a Socket.IO event to notify subscribers upon successful addition.

        h3 5. Delete a Currency Rate (JWT Required)
        p
            | Enables an authenticated user to delete a specific currency rate using its unique identifier.
            | Only the uploader or a designated admin can perform this operation.
        p
            strong DELETE /delete/:id
        p Example URL:
            strong
                a(href="#{baseUrl}delete/64e8d3f2a2b7b2a5c1f12345") #{baseUrl}delete/64e8d3f2a2b7b2a5c1f12345

        p Notes:
        ul
            li Returns HTTP 403 if a user attempts to delete a rate uploaded by another user.
            li Returns HTTP 204 if deletion is successful.

        h3 6. Retrieve a Currency Rate by ID (Includes Percentage Change)
        p
            | Retrieves a single currency rate by its unique identifier, along with the calculated percentage change compared to the most recent previous rate for the same currency, unit, source, and uploader.
        p
            strong GET /:id
        p Example URL:
            strong
                a(href="#{baseUrl}68aebc40a6e743a5b92498b6") #{baseUrl}68aebc40a6e743a5b92498b6

        p Notes:
        ul
            li Percentage change is computed relative to the most recent previous rate for the same currency, unit, source, and uploader.
            li Returns HTTP 404 if the specified ID is not found.

        h3 7. Retrieve the Latest Currency Rate
        p
            | Fetches the most recent currency rate for a specific currency or for all currencies from a given source and uploader.
        p
            strong GET /:currencyCode/latest?source=&uploader=
        p Single currency example:
            strong
                a(href="#{baseUrl}USD/latest?source=MM Exchange&uploader=admin123") #{baseUrl}USD/latest?source=MM Exchange&uploader=admin123
        p All currencies example:
            strong
                a(href="#{baseUrl}ALL/latest?source=MM Exchange&uploader=admin123") #{baseUrl}ALL/latest?source=MM Exchange&uploader=admin123

        p Notes:
        ul
            li Use `ALL` as the `currencyCode` to fetch the latest rates for all currencies.
            li Returns HTTP 404 if no rate is found for the specified currency/source/uploader combination.

        h3 8. Retrieve Currency Rate by Date
        p
            | Fetches currency rates for a specified date. This endpoint supports retrieval of a single currency or all currencies and allows pagination using `skip` and `limit` query parameters.
        p
            strong GET /:currencyCode/:date?skip=0&limit=10
        p Single currency example:
            strong
                a(href="#{baseUrl}USD/2025-08-27?source=MM Exchange&uploader=admin123&skip=0&limit=10") #{baseUrl}USD/2025-08-27?source=MM Exchange&uploader=admin123&skip=0&limit=10
        p All currencies example:
            strong
                a(href="#{baseUrl}ALL/2025-08-27?source=MM Exchange&uploader=admin123&skip=0&limit=10") #{baseUrl}ALL/2025-08-27?source=MM Exchange&uploader=admin123&skip=0&limit=10

        p Notes:
        ul
            li Supports pagination through `skip` and `limit` parameters.
            li Returns HTTP 404 if no rates exist for the given date.
            li Dates are interpreted in the Asia/Yangon timezone.

        h3 9. Retrieve Currency Rate Count by Date
        p
            | Returns the total number of currency rates available for a specific currency on a given date.
            | Optional query parameters allow filtering by source and uploader.
        p
            strong GET /count/:currencyCode/:date
        p Example URL:
            strong
                a(href="#{baseUrl}count/USD/2025-08-27?source=MM Exchange&uploader=admin123") #{baseUrl}count/USD/2025-08-27?source=MM Exchange&uploader=admin123

        p Notes:
        ul
            li Returns zero if no rates exist for the specified currency and date.

        h3 10. Retrieve Currency Rates Between Two Dates
        p
            | Retrieves currency rates for a specified period between two dates. Can fetch a single currency or all currencies. Supports pagination via `skip` and `limit`.
        p
            strong GET /:currencyCode/:fromDate/:toDate?skip=0&limit=10
        p Single currency example:
            strong
                a(href="#{baseUrl}USD/2025-08-01/2025-08-27?source=MM Exchange&uploader=admin123&skip=0&limit=10") #{baseUrl}USD/2025-08-01/2025-08-27?source=MM Exchange&uploader=admin123&skip=0&limit=10
        p All currencies example:
            strong
                a(href="#{baseUrl}ALL/2025-08-01/2025-08-27?source=MM Exchange&uploader=admin123&skip=0&limit=10") #{baseUrl}ALL/2025-08-01/2025-08-27?source=MM Exchange&uploader=admin123&skip=0&limit=10

        p Notes:
        ul
            li Date range is inclusive.
            li Returns HTTP 404 if no rates exist within the specified period.
            li Supports pagination through `skip` and `limit`.
            li Dates are interpreted in the Asia/Yangon timezone.

        h3 11. Retrieve Currency Rate Count Between Two Dates
        p
            | Returns the total number of currency rates available between two specified dates for a given currency. Optional filters for source and uploader may be applied.
        p
            strong GET /count/:currencyCode/:fromDate/:toDate
        p Example URL:
            strong
                a(href="#{baseUrl}count/USD/2025-08-01/2025-08-27?source=MM Exchange&uploader=admin123") #{baseUrl}count/USD/2025-08-01/2025-08-27?source=MM Exchange&uploader=admin123

        h2 General Notes
        ul
            li All dates and times are handled in the Asia/Yangon timezone.
            li The `uploadedDate` field must not be set to a future timestamp.
            li Parameters `skip` and `limit` are used for pagination. `skip` specifies the number of records to skip, `limit` specifies the maximum number of records returned.
            li Many GET endpoints are cached for 60 seconds to optimize performance; cache automatically refreshes when underlying data changes.
            li Percentage change values are calculated relative to the most recent previous rate for the same currency, unit, source, and uploader.
